## Deployment Plan

[timeline color=green]
- Sep 22: Shadow mode — v4.3 runs alongside v3.9 LSTM, outputs logged but not acted on
- Sep 29: A/B test begins — 20% of CS intervention triggers routed through new model scores
- Oct 6: A/B readout — if precision holds at >87%, full cutover approved by ML lead
- Oct 10: Full production cutover — v3.9 LSTM retired, v4.3 becomes primary
- Oct 17: Post-deploy review — false positive rate, CS feedback, and churn impact measured
[/timeline]

[section title="Risks & Mitigations" style=card]

[alert type=warning text="Model trained on 18 months data — may underperform for accounts <90 days old (7% of base). Separate early-lifecycle model v4.5-LR recommended for this cohort."]
[alert type=info text="SMOTE oversampling improves recall on churned class but slightly inflates precision in test set. Monitored with 30-day post-deploy precision tracking dashboard."]

[list style=check]
- Shadow mode gate: precision must be >85% on live data before A/B launch
- Rollback plan ready: feature flag toggles back to v3.9 within 30 seconds
- Bias audit complete: no significant performance gap across company size, industry, or geo
[/list]

[/section]
